            "bodyHtml": "<div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg\" width=\"300\" height=\"402.6\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:671,&quot;width&quot;:500,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:300,&quot;bytes&quot;:null,&quot;alt&quot;:&quot;34 ideias de Botas | arte em pintura, botas velhas, pintura em tela&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:null,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:false,&quot;topImage&quot;:true,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:null,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"34 ideias de Botas | arte em pintura, botas velhas, pintura em tela\" title=\"34 ideias de Botas | arte em pintura, botas velhas, pintura em tela\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r-dS!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa00df628-de99-4c10-9840-0332504a8b56_500x671.jpeg 1456w\" sizes=\"100vw\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></picture></div></a></figure></div><p><em>Manaus, AM - Saturday, May 9, 2026, 4:35pm</em></p><p>I found a definition I recently found interesting about the difference between emotion and feeling. I share below some notes and reflections on the topic.</p><p><strong>Emotion is born first</strong></p><p>Emotion is automatic and unconscious [1]. It appears as a response to a stimulus, before we are even able to completely rationalize what is happening. In many cases, the body reacts before the mind organizes a conscious interpretation of the situation.</p><p><strong>The feeling comes later</strong></p><p>The feeling is born when we recognize, interpret and attribute meaning to the emotion that was already happening internally [1]. This distinction seems simple at first glance, but it helps explain why we often react before understanding exactly what we are feeling.</p><p><strong>Universal emotions</strong></p><p>Another interesting point is that, despite cultural, social and individual differences, there are emotions considered universal [2]:</p><ul><li><p>Happiness</p></li><li><p>Sadness</p></li><li><p>Fear</p></li><li><p>Anger</p></li><li><p>Aversion (disgust)</p></li><li><p>Surprise</p></li><li><p>Contempt</p></li></ul><p>These emotions usually manifest themselves through facial microexpressions that are recognized in very similar ways in different parts of the world[3].</p><p><strong>References</strong></p><p>[1] António Damásio – emotion, feeling and decision making<br><a href=\"https://www.fronteiras.com/leia/exibir/emocao-ou-sentimento-mental-ou-comportamental-antonio-damasio-explica-a-organizacao-afetiva-humana\">https://www.fronteiras.com/leia/exibir/emocao-ou-sentimento-mental-ou-comportamental-antonio-damasio-explica-a-organizacao-afetiva-humana</a></p><p>[2] Paul Ekman – universal emotions<br><a href=\"https://www.paulekman.com/universal-emotions/\">https://www.paulekman.com/universal-emotions/</a></p><p>[3] Paul Ekman – microexpressions<br><a href=\"https://www.paulekman.com/resources/micro-expressions/\">https://www.paulekman.com/resources/micro-expressions/</a></p><p>Yours sincerely,<br>Mateus Lucena</p><p></p>"
